# The storefront order board. Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# This app is deployed once per platform, not per tenant: tenancy comes from
# the location on the URL and the brand config it resolves. What is per-screen
# is the device token below.

# The Supabase project. Public, and only ever read through board_tickets.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# The paired display device's token, issued from the HQ console
# (Locations -> Devices -> Connect a display). NOT the anon/publishable key:
# migration 0033 gates board_tickets on app.can_read_board, which admits a
# paired display device, a brand owner, or staff at the location -- and the
# anon key is none of those. With the anon key the read succeeds, returns zero
# rows, and the board renders an empty queue labelled "Live", which is the one
# failure this surface must never have.
#
# Without this, a production build shows an honest "not paired" screen.
#
# This token lasts twelve hours. On a wall in a shop that is a fixed end: half a
# day after the deploy the queue goes dark and the only remedy is a human
# editing this value. Prefer the refresh secret below and leave this unset.
DISPLAY_DEVICE_TOKEN=

# The durable credential, and the one to use. Issued once from the HQ console
# (Locations -> Devices -> Issue refresh secret; POST /api/devices/refresh-secret).
# The screen trades it for a twelve-hour token whenever one is needed, so it
# survives a deploy, a power cut and a night switched off. Only its HMAC is
# stored, so this value is shown once and revoking the device clears it.
#
# HQ_ORIGIN below must also be set: the secret is exchanged against HQ, and a
# secret with nowhere to exchange it mints nothing.
DISPLAY_DEVICE_REFRESH_SECRET=

# Optional. Draws the demo queue -- invented guests, a moving cycle -- in a
# production build. For a trade stand or a sales call. Never in a shop: the
# names are fabricated and the room cannot tell.
# DISPLAY_DEMO_MODE=1

# Local five-surface wall only. The client refuses non-loopback URLs, and the
# HQ demo-sync route is disabled in production. Do not set this on a deployed display.
# DEMO_SYNC_URL=http://localhost:3300/api/demo-sync
# PREVIEW_WALL=1

# The only production parent allowed to embed this display in HQ. Set this to
# the canonical HQ origin when the console uses a custom domain. The value is
# read by next.config.ts when the display is built.
# HQ_ORIGIN=https://coffee-story-hq.vercel.app
# HQ_ORIGIN also receives server-side display telemetry. DISPLAY_DEVICE_TOKEN
# remains on this server and is never included in pickup-board browser code.

# Optional. Errors and degraded reads go here; without it the board reports
# nothing to anyone, and nobody is watching a wall for a fault.
# SENTRY_DSN=
